lly posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473175#post473175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how much of this game would be unchanged rules stuff? Obviously a mummy's not going to be a Junior, and a Promethean wouldn't be able to stay in a school for an entire year with regular classes (and thus interacting with the same people at least daily, if not more frequently).<br /> <br /> I think before getting to a Storyteller, we need to figure out how much of the rules, Affinities, Disciplines, Merits, etc... need to be altered to fit within the framework.</div> </div> </div> </div>A mummy can be a freshman if they've got a young enough body. Twice Arisen happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T12:38:57-07:00","id":473226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473222#post473222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>That's</b> a <i>High School?</i><b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Of course! It's the Xavier institute for gifted youngsters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T12:40:37-07:00","id":473229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473222#post473222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>That's</b> a <i>High School?</i><b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Technically it also has a prepatory school, so it covers from children age 8 and up as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T12:44:17-07:00","id":473232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473224#post473224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mummy can be a freshman if they've got a young enough body. Twice Arisen happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of make's Edward's problems seem minor...<br /> <br /> I guess I'm just saying we should find a page to stay consistent with regarding our characters. For instance, if somebody wants to play a Created, obviously we'll have to change up the rules for Disquiet and wasteland, unless we want to play in a school that's slowly but surely deteriorating all year and half of the student body wants to run one of the students out.<br /> <br /> What gameplay, themes, etc... from core NWoD are we replacing with high school tropes to make the game playable and &quot;long-term&quot; plausible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T13:32:13-07:00","id":473281,"title":"","content":"Will the school be inner city or suburban? private or public? If private, is it a special supernatural school or mostly normal? are we setting it in a real town or fictional? Are we doing 2nd edition or 1st?<br /> <br /> And I might play in this, it would be my first time playing however. If I do play, then I am thinking an Iron Master Cahalith sophomore film geek in the AV club with a YouTube channel that he hopes will pay for film school.<br /> <br /> In regard to tropes... I think that maybe we should tone down how powerful the older supernaturals are, since a big part of high school stories is that most of the adults are useless at helping the characters with their problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T15:18:12-07:00","id":473415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473281#post473281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the school be inner city or suburban? private or public? If private, is it a special supernatural school or mostly normal? are we setting it in a real town or fictional? Are we doing 2nd edition or 1st?<br /> <br /> And I might play in this, it would be my first time playing however. If I do play, then I am thinking an Iron Master Cahalith sophomore film geek in the AV club with a YouTube channel that he hopes will pay for film school.<br /> <br /> In regard to tropes... I think that maybe we should tone down how powerful the older supernaturals are, since a big part of high school stories is that most of the adults are useless at helping the characters with their problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>We should use second edition books seeing as they are more updated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T15:26:13-07:00","id":473427,"title":"","content":"Technically, wouldn't we be able to avoid Wasteland progression by having any Prommies come in from a great enough distance?<br /> <br /> I mean, you'd have 8 hours' worth of Wasteland effects build up, then there'd be 16 hours for it to disperse when they go home.<br /> <br /> I actually had an idea a while back about a throng of Created living in an RV that just moves the minimum required distance (10 miles IIRC) to avoid Wasteland progression before it can get past Stage 1 every hour. Circle around and xome back to its startinf point once enough time's passed to reset the Wasteland. Might work for this game.<br /> <br /> As for Disquiet... Well, I imagine a Mastigos mage could probably mitigate it somewhat at least.<br /> <br /> Also: Principal Principle is a thing that must happen. The God-Machine is clearly the school's custodian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 04-08-2015, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T15:30:54-07:00","id":473432,"title":"","content":"Is the Masquerade something we need to worry about? Or are all the students pretty much free to let their (supernatural) freak flags fly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T15:53:08-07:00","id":473463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473432#post473432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Masquerade something we need to worry about? Or are all the students pretty much free to let their (supernatural) freak flags fly?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which brings up another point, this should probably be a night school... so the vampire kids can stay awake in class... or don't burst into flames mid lecture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:01:26-07:00","id":473623,"title":"","content":"1) A Promethean can survive a year of high school.<br /> 2) ...I got nothing on Vampires.<br /> 3) I assume the Masquerade is in effect.<br /> <br /> Unless this is like Matt's suggestion of a darker and heavier Hotel Transylvania turned school.<br /> <br /> Or Xavier's school, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:06:32-07:00","id":473647,"title":"","content":"I vote we make that Mastigos girl the prom queen this year... then dump pigs blood on her!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:11:42-07:00","id":473650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473647#post473647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vote we make that Mastigos girl the prom queen this year... then dump pigs blood on her!</div> </div> </div> </div>I vote we skip prom, hit a nice restaurant in a town the next county over, and learn how that turned out on the 11 O'Clock news. We can even get a beat for fulfilling our aspiration of not doing anything stupid for at least a week!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:20:45-07:00","id":473654,"title":"","content":"We're playing teenagers. I've pretty sure your constant aspiration is unintended stupidity at that age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:38:55-07:00","id":473677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473281#post473281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the school be inner city or suburban? private or public? If private, is it a special supernatural school or mostly normal? are we setting it in a real town or fictional? Are we doing 2nd edition or 1st?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly private. If you have very, <i>very</i> special needs child you probably want to fly as far below the governments radar as possible, and besides, a lot of these kids are going to be old money anyway. No public school is going to accept roman denarii as tuition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473281#post473281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regard to tropes... I think that maybe we should tone down how powerful the older supernaturals are, since a big part of high school stories is that most of the adults are useless at helping the characters with their problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473427#post473427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: Principal Principle is a thing that must happen. The God-Machine is clearly the school's custodian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes for the Principal. I disagree with the G-M as custodian; It needs to be remote, unseen and utterly disconnected from the needs of the school and the student body. I recommend the board of directors or the PTA.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473432#post473432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Masquerade something we need to worry about? Or are all the students pretty much free to let their (supernatural) freak flags fly?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Masquerade is in effect. Most of the students of all splats have extensive reasons why they stay hidden (Vampire has Masquerade, Werewolf has Oath of the Moon, Changelings don\u2019t want to be dragged off to Arcadia) and there\u2019s comic gold in a school full of supernaturals stubbornly pretending that Everything Is Normal even as the cheerleading captain bathes in the blood of her ex-boyfriend and sets the school tennis court on fire &quot;as is foretold in the prophecy&quot; during the throes of kuruth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473654#post473654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're playing teenagers. I've pretty sure your constant aspiration is unintended stupidity at that age.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, but my original vote stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:56:01-07:00","id":473708,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one for this happening in a regular school?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T20:02:37-07:00","id":473748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473708#post473708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one for this happening in a regular school?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean where only the party members and a handful of Storyteller characters are supernatural and maybe the Principle Principal?<br /> <br /> And the Masquerade would be in full effect? Guess that means we need daylight vampires then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T20:04:49-07:00","id":473750,"title":"","content":"Or they could just be the 'bad kids', or something, or the ones you see at the movies or something but not in school because [insert illness/family emergency/work issues/etc].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T20:24:01-07:00","id":473778,"title":"","content":"Or the Breakfast Club.<br /> <br /> Carmilla has perfected the art of daysleeping with her eyes open.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T20:44:41-07:00","id":473795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473463#post473463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Which brings up another point, this should probably be a night school... so the vampire kids can stay awake in class... or don't burst into flames mid lecture.</div> </div> </div> </div>We could always handwave that. Or we could argue that sunscreen is sufficient for the length of a school day. Although, if we don't just hack it away, that does seem important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T21:09:40-07:00","id":473815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473677#post473677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes for the Principal. I disagree with the G-M as custodian; It needs to be remote, unseen and utterly disconnected from the needs of the school and the student body. I recommend the board of directors or the PTA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, mysterious head custodian that nobody ever actually sees. There's a custodial staff that reports to him, but there appears to be a REALLY high turnover rate. The students swear they literally pop out of the walls, do one job, and then disappear. Literally.<br /> <br /> Also, the school is ALWAYS under construction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/P_DgJ8R-8XI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/P_DgJ8R-8XI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/P_DgJ8R-8XI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/P_DgJ8R-8XI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Note that a custodian is not the same thing as a janitor. Custodians are more along the lines of handymen/contractors than cleaners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T21:15:50-07:00","id":473821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473815#post473815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, mysterious head custodian that nobody ever actually sees. There's a custodial staff that reports to him, but there appears to be a REALLY high turnover rate. The students swear they literally pop out of the walls, do one job, and then disappear. Literally.<br /> <br /> Also, the school is ALWAYS under construction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/P_DgJ8R-8XI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/P_DgJ8R-8XI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/P_DgJ8R-8XI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/P_DgJ8R-8XI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Note that a custodian is not the same thing as a janitor. Custodians are more along the lines of handymen/contractors than cleaners.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I attended a high school which half of it burned down. Instead of repairing the damage, they just locked the section off and left it to rot. When I tried peering through the windows, it looked like the class rooms were for elementary school kids, not highschoolers, so I guess it got repurposed. The abandoned sections were fucking creepy enough on the outside, and I wasn't about to sneak around inside!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T21:16:10-07:00","id":473822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473748#post473748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean where only the party members and a handful of Storyteller characters are supernatural and maybe the Principle Principal?<br /> <br /> And the Masquerade would be in full effect? Guess that means we need daylight vampires then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't neonates operate in daylight to a limited degree as long as they keep their Humanity high? They should be fine so long as they stay away from the windows and don't dawdle between classes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T02:14:46-07:00","id":474006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=473708#post473708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one for this happening in a regular school?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it could be cool to see a mix of both regular people and supernaturals in that school- and that the normal ones don't know about the supernatural ones. Heck, maybe even the supernatural ones don't know about the supernatural ones. It gives place to all kind of teenage drama and rumors about other students and teachers (like, everyone say that the creepy goth guy is weird. Everyone who talks with him get hurt. Only that he is a regular guy, and that the fault is in the popular sin eater who use him as a scape goat. That is, until he Awakens and decide to make the false rumors into real ones)<br /> <br /> Also, nice to see you returned to that avatar Arc. It was always my fave :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T05:05:53-07:00","id":474124,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if it's a &quot;normal&quot; school that just happens to have a bunch of supernaturals then vampires need to be addressed. Them and Prometheans. I don't think anybody else really needs special consideration.<br /> <br /> Just letting the vampires move about in the daylight, perhaps with some sort of &quot;Lethargic&quot; Condition that prevents them from healing properly or using some Disciplines, seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> For the Created, Disquiet doesn't need to be changed: their teachers all think that they're cheating and their regular classmates hate them.<br /> <br /> Either the supernaturals should just know about each other or abilities that let you detect supers should be nixed. In a small environment those abilities would ruin the suspense of who is or who isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T05:18:05-07:00","id":474132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474124#post474124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, if it's a &quot;normal&quot; school that just happens to have a bunch of supernaturals then vampires need to be addressed. Them and Prometheans. I don't think anybody else really needs special consideration.<br /> <br /> Just letting the vampires move about in the daylight, perhaps with some sort of &quot;Lethargic&quot; Condition that prevents them from healing properly or using some Disciplines, seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> For the Created, Disquiet doesn't need to be changed: their teachers all think that they're cheating and their regular classmates hate them.<br /> <br /> Either the supernaturals should just know about each other or abilities that let you detect supers should be nixed. In a small environment those abilities would ruin the suspense of who is or who isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Low BP vampires would be more or less fine with the rules as is, given that the indoors ain't too accesable by sun :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T06:10:44-07:00","id":474184,"title":"","content":"Here is my mock up of the logo I hope this works<br /> <br /> Blank Page <a href=\"http://i292.photobucket.com/albums/mm19/6threalm/NWoDBorder%20High%20School_zpshnjmz0hu.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i292.photobucket.com/albums/m...pshnjmz0hu.jpg</a><br /> <br /> Logo <a href=\"http://i292.photobucket.com/albums/mm19/6threalm/HighSchool_zpsleofy4ec.png\" target=\"_blank\">http://i292.photobucket.com/albums/m...psleofy4ec.png</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":3293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","user":"Rahod","date":". 04-09-2015, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:24:23-07:00","id":474539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474124#post474124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, if it's a &quot;normal&quot; school that just happens to have a bunch of supernaturals then vampires need to be addressed.<br /> Just letting the vampires move about in the daylight, perhaps with some sort of &quot;Lethargic&quot; Condition that prevents them from healing properly or using some Disciplines, seems appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's pretty much how vampires in the original folklore were. They were able to go out in sunlight without bursting into flames, but it weakened them to do so and they couldn't use their vampire abilities. The fact is that vampires bursting into flames in sunlight was invented by Hollywood, so I'm cool with ditching it in this campaign..<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:26:14-07:00","id":474543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474132#post474132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Low BP vampires would be more or less fine with the rules as is, given that the indoors ain't too accesable by sun :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how new the school building is. The trend with newer schools is sunlighting, which is education worker speak for putting as many windows in the classrooms as possible because studies show that sunlight boosts academic performance (at least in non-vampires)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:28:20-07:00","id":474545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474543#post474543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on how new the school building is. The trend with newer schools is sunlighting, which is education worker speak for putting as many windows in the classrooms as possible because studies show that sunlight boosts academic performance (at least in non-vampires)</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of like the idea of the school being older, and reasonably more Gothic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:54:45-07:00","id":474631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474545#post474545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of like the idea of the school being older, and reasonably more Gothic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't: This is the NWoD, not the OWoD. Embrace modernity and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T12:25:03-07:00","id":474694,"title":"","content":"How about both? An Old Gothic School in the middle of a massive renovation, replacing buildings with modern ones, creating an off-putting, anachronistic, and syncretic environment that embodies the confusion of growing up as well as sets the stage for quite a few conflicts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T12:26:57-07:00","id":474697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474631#post474631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't: This is the NWoD, not the OWoD. Embrace modernity and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>EDIT: I didn't read Arcane's post before posting this one. I agree with Arcane, old school in the middle of renovations is wonderful.<br /> <br /> Now let's talk about the educational theories the school staff follow. If only because the school's polices could create story hooks<br /> If this is a modern private school for rich supernatural kids, then I imagine that it avoids some of the mistakes often made by public school system and is embracing the latest trends in education in part because they have the money needed to do things right.<br /> <br /> For instance, many school are adopting a program where instead of Fs students get Hs, which means that the student will be given a chance to complete the assignment right (either during study hall after school or even during Saturday school). The idea is that it gives failing students a chance to catch up. A group of students having to make up an assignment they got an H on after school could easliy be a hook for a story<br /> <br /> Also, year round school might be a thing at this school, many schools are doing a year round deal where you get a 15 day break for every 45 days you go to school. The idea is that it makes it so the teachers don't have to waste time reteaching everything that was forgotten over the summer while still having the same number of school days. Ultimatly, this is so that we can have vacation adventures outside of spring, winter and summer break and so that any summer court changlings don't feel left out of the school hi jinks.<br /> <br /> Oh and the cafeteria! the dietary needs of some the students could lead to some interesting. stuff I have an idea of the blood substitute variety that could be served there, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire_pumpkins_and_watermelons\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire watermelons</a> (I'm serious). Some of you may have heard of these from the DiscWorld books, but the late great Sir Terry didn't come up with them himself. A produce of Romani folklore, these fruit leak blood, roll around on their own and make a sound like &quot;Brrl brrl&quot;. So what I am think is that rather than being vampires that are watermelons, they are watermelons altered to make human blood instead of watermelon juice. What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 04-09-2015, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T12:48:00-07:00","id":474728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474694#post474694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about both? An Old Gothic School in the middle of a massive renovation, replacing buildings with modern ones, creating an off-putting, anachronistic, and syncretic environment that embodies the confusion of growing up as well as sets the stage for quite a few conflicts?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point. You have softened this young man's hard heart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474697#post474697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For instance, many school are adopting a program where instead of Fs students get Hs, which means that the student will be given a chance to complete the assignment right (either during study hall after school or even during Saturday school). The idea is that it gives failing students a chance to catch up. A group of students having to make up an assignment they got an H on after school could easliy be a hook for a story<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but even in real-life there's the Bill &amp; Ted caveat where &quot;If you fail this project you fail the course.&quot; May not be realistic, but it's cinematic and more tense than makeup stuff. I'd rather take a <i>Breakfast Club</i> approach and make the hook &quot;in Detention&quot; than &quot;studying/doing makeup work&quot; because there aren't any requirements in Detention. Maybe you use the opportunity to work on homework, but overall it gives you a place to be and an authority figure to rally against with shenanigans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474697#post474697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, year round school might be a thing at this school, many schools are doing a year round deal where you get a 15 day break for every 45 days you go to school. The idea is that it makes it so the teachers don't have to waste time reteaching everything that was forgotten over the summer while still having the same number of school days. Ultimatly, this is so that we can have vacation adventures outside of spring, winter and summer break and so that any summer court changlings don't feel left out of the school hi jinks.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I generally like this, though don't discount the American way of having a huge summer break: that's an important cultural touchstone to consider. I'm not saying that we <i>have</i>to use that one, just that we should consider our options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474697#post474697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh and the cafeteria! the dietary needs of some the students could lead to some interesting. stuff I have an idea of the blood substitute variety that could be served there, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire_pumpkins_and_watermelons\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire watermelons</a> (I'm serious). Some of you may have heard of these from the DiscWorld books, but the late great Sir Terry didn't come up with them himself. A produce of Romani folklore, these fruit leak blood, roll around on their own and make a sound like &quot;Brrl brrl&quot;. So what I am think is that rather than being vampires that are watermelons, they are watermelons altered to make human blood instead of watermelon juice. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>This goes back to what we were saying about whether or not this is a &quot;normal&quot; school, though.<br /> <br /> I think I prefer the &quot;This is a regular school, but there are a handful of supernatural students and teachers who keep it a secret from the regular population.&quot; approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T12:55:21-07:00","id":474735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474728#post474728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This goes back to what we were saying about whether or not this is a &quot;normal&quot; school, though.<br /> <br /> I think I prefer the &quot;This is a regular school, but there are a handful of supernatural students and teachers who keep it a secret from the regular population.&quot; approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't mean they can't have the blood melons in the cafeteria. If there are &quot;normal' students at the school, then they probably serve the melon juice in cans from the cafeteria soda machine and call it something that sounds like a fruit juice drink (I'll let you guys come up with the brand name). Almost everyone who has drank it says it's disgusting and a few students say it made them sick, but it has a small group of students who drink the stuff every lunch period. In fact, they never seem to eat or drink anything else.<br /> <br /> Also, is this private school a boarding school? or are the parents still part of the picture. Or is it both, a boarding school where some the students parents live in town and are still a presence in those student's lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:02:32-07:00","id":474771,"title":"","content":"There's also the fact that if you give the vampire students an accessible means of rejuvenating their Vitae, then it takes a lot of tension out of the game by removing the need to make feeding rolls.<br /> <br /> Oh I'm sure you could justify making them from time to time, like after a big encounter, or if they've gone without for a while. But again, there's no reason for them to go without if they can just spend the $2.35 to buy a Vitae or two.<br /> <br /> Boarding school question's a good one. As are parents. I think some supers probably just don't have parents around as a rule (most Prometheans, Mummies, Demons, Changelings). Though those may have equivalents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:05:31-07:00","id":474790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474735#post474735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'll let you guys come up with the brand name)</div> </div> </div> </div>Clamato Juice. We're calling it Clamato Juice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:07:29-07:00","id":474791,"title":"","content":"Well. some boarding schools (like the one I went to) also had 'day students' - ones who went back home eah evening and night like regular school kids. You might just have the 'weird' students all be full boarders","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:09:14-07:00","id":474792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474771#post474771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the fact that if you give the vampire students an accessible means of rejuvenating their Vitae, then it takes a lot of tension out of the game by removing the need to make feeding rolls.<br /> <br /> Oh I'm sure you could justify making them from time to time, like after a big encounter, or if they've gone without for a while. But again, there's no reason for them to go without if they can just spend the $2.35 to buy a Vitae or two.<br /> <br /> Boarding school question's a good one. As are parents. I think some supers probably just don't have parents around as a rule (most Prometheans, Mummies, Demons, Changelings). Though those may have equivalents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was kind of thinking that figuring out just who is making the Vitae in can, and some paranoia as to if the Vitae in can is part of a nefarious purpose, could replace that tension. As in, the Vitae in a can is convenient, but it has weird side effects on the vampires who drink it. It is an east way to get Vitae, but in the WoD, the easy way always has a horrible price. Hey, if I get called to take a turn story telling, I may have just found my plot.<br /> <br /> But I think you might be right about the parents, though I think that a demiurge could be the equivalent for Prometheans, a teenage mummy might have members of their cult acting as their parents for legal purposes, A demon might have a cover as the child of the covers of other demons and changelings could be assumed to have pulled off the kill and replace their fetch trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 04-09-2015, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:34:13-07:00","id":474852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474792#post474792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was kind of thinking that figuring out just who is making the Vitae in can, and some paranoia as to if the Vitae in can is part of a nefarious purpose, could replace that tension. As in, the Vitae in a can is convenient, but it has weird side effects on the vampires who drink it. It is an east way to get Vitae, but in the WoD, the easy way always has a horrible price. Hey, if I get called to take a turn story telling, I may have just found my plot.<br /> <br /> But I think you might be right about the parents, though I think that a demiurge could be the equivalent for Prometheans, a teenage mummy might have members of their cult acting as their parents for legal purposes, A demon might have a cover as the child of the covers of other demons and changelings could be assumed to have pulled off the kill and replace their fetch trick.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Kindred blood.<br /> <br /> Someone is trying to force Vinculae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:51:02-07:00","id":474885,"title":"","content":"I feel like I need to provide a perspective on the whole vampire thing, sooooooo.....questions on that.<br /> <br /> 1) Do we even have anyone intent on playing a vampire in a high school setting? If we don't, then...don't worry about it. No vampires in the play group means we can open it up to either being a vanilla school or a school for supernaturals, where if vampires have to be in there, we either have to change the setting details on vampire, or we need a school that handles their issues, which answers a number of questions. It's probably a boarding school, someone is probably doing some kind of experimentation with shaping the supernatural populace, etc. Of course, this is all assuming that the teen vampire has to be in high school, soooooooooooooo............<br /> <br /> 2) Are we interested in vampires <i>actually</i> being in school, or are we interested in vampires being part of the teenage experience? A vampire can be home-schooled, but they can be involved with people from the school.<br /> <br /> A big part about supernaturals in a high school setting is a <i>really hard hit</i> on the damage teens do to each other just stumbling through. I favor the normal school with parental involvement and a not very well watched environment supernaturally speaking. Vampires <i>should</i> have to chase down their fellows.<br /> <br /> In regards to the school and it's policies....I need to eat, I'll get back to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:55:43-07:00","id":474887,"title":"","content":"I mean, if there's a problem with losing tension and/or you want an arc that can be shared with other STs, just introduce a stoner Greek home-schooled kid. He brings a family Relic to school to try to win friends and misplaces it. &quot;It's Greek to me, haha bro. What, Attic Greek? I mean I found it in my Attic, ya. It says 'Book of Pure Evil'? Right on!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2583-amikaligula","name":"amikaligula","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T14:26:21-07:00","id":474898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474885#post474885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I need to provide a perspective on the whole vampire thing, sooooooo.....questions on that.<br /> <br /> 1) Do we even have anyone intent on playing a vampire in a high school setting? If we don't, then...don't worry about it. No vampires in the play group means we can open it up to either being a vanilla school or a school for supernaturals, where if vampires have to be in there, we either have to change the setting details on vampire, or we need a school that handles their issues, which answers a number of questions. It's probably a boarding school, someone is probably doing some kind of experimentation with shaping the supernatural populace, etc. Of course, this is all assuming that the teen vampire has to be in high school, soooooooooooooo............<br /> <br /> 2) Are we interested in vampires <i>actually</i> being in school, or are we interested in vampires being part of the teenage experience? A vampire can be home-schooled, but they can be involved with people from the school.<br /> <br /> A big part about supernaturals in a high school setting is a <i>really hard hit</i> on the damage teens do to each other just stumbling through. I favor the normal school with parental involvement and a not very well watched environment supernaturally speaking. Vampires <i>should</i> have to chase down their fellows.<br /> <br /> In regards to the school and it's policies....I need to eat, I'll get back to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Arcane's right, we should figure out if anyone WANTS to play a vampire before we start talking about them.<br /> <br /> Also, can the parents be supernatural? not saying they shouldn't still be useless, but that doesn't mean they don't know about the supernatural, they just don't think their kids's problerms are a big deal compared to their own drama. Maybe the parents are the PCs of their own campaign (not literally, but in the sense that they are the heroes of a different story) and don't have time to take care of their own problems and those of their kids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T14:50:44-07:00","id":474920,"title":"","content":"That falls on individual characters. I agree with Matt(You know, Black Hat Matt) when he says that having mentor figures(read supernatural parents) kind of kills the confusion and isolation metaphor you have as a teenager(Which, considering Promethean spoke to me as a teenager, is true as fuck), but fecking hell, it's y'alls characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T15:03:47-07:00","id":474943,"title":"","content":"My first instinct is saying that the parents should be more of a background characters- something that doesn't come up much in the game itself. Maybe some parents are more &quot;famous&quot; then the others, but in the core most of the NPCs the protagonists are going to deal with in game should be, IMO, others students or teachers. Involving the parents should be used as some sort of Deus Ex Machina- that is, they would get involved only if things get really out of control. Just think about it- how many teenagers actually include their parents as an active part of their school life from their free will?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T15:08:54-07:00","id":474948,"title":"","content":"Parents, in a high school setting, should exist for one reason and one reason only:<br /> <br /> They should make everything worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T15:13:36-07:00","id":474950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474920#post474920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That falls on individual characters. I agree with Matt(You know, Black Hat Matt) when he says that having mentor figures(read supernatural parents) kind of kills the confusion and isolation metaphor you have as a teenager(Which, considering Promethean spoke to me as a teenager, is true as fuck), but fecking hell, it's y'alls characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I am thinking is that my character is one of the students who lives at the boarding school. His parents are both werewolves, but they live in a different state. So they don't really act as mentors. In fact his relationship with them is very dysfunctional.<br /> <br /> Plus I imagine that I need to buff up on the confusion and isolation metaphor because I'm not sure how I would be able to handle roleplaying the relationship drama element of high school. You see, I am both an asexual AND austistic, so not only do I not have an instinctive understanding of human interaction, but I don't understand human sexual behavior very well.<br /> <br /> But now that I think about it, being asexual really amped up the confusion and isolation of high school for me, since so much teenage behavior and culture was screaming blood and tears soaked nonsense for me in high school AND I was worried about what people would think if I &quot;came out&quot; as not being interested in other people sexually/romanticly, since one thing I read when I researched the topic is that most people don't think we exist and the people who do, think there is something mentally wrong with us (the phrases &quot;cold&quot; and &quot;animalistic&quot; are used a lot to describe us) (and that's when we aren't being mistaken for closeted homosexuals).<br /> <br /> Plus, I like the idea of a teenage supernatural who who defies genre convention by not being interested in romance or even noticing when people are hitting on him.<br /> <br /> EDIT: While my RL family (except for my dad) is okay with me being asexual. I imagine it could be why my character's relationship with his family is so messed up. See, while my char is an Iron Master Cahalith, his parents are Pure. His father is an Ivory Claw and his mother is a Fire Touched from a Claw bloodline. He was sent to the school after his parent's arranged marriage ended in a nasty divorce and defected to the Forsaken in his freshmen year (I remember reading in tribes of the moon is that Pure who never had an auspice get whatever auspice they would have had if it weren't for that Pure rite that hides them from Luna when that defect.). His parents don't know he switched sides and, because his father assumes that he is just an allosexual (Asexual term for people who do feel attraction to other people) who hasn't &quot;activated&quot; yet, he is constantly having to deal with pesky Ivory Claw suitors that his father keeps sending his way. This, of course, is not good for my char since these suitors might realize that he is Forsaken and tell his parents. What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 04-09-2015, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T15:54:07-07:00","id":475000,"title":"","content":"I think I want to run a Sin-Eater who's a hopeless romantic. Unfortunately, he happens to be sharing his body with a Geist known as the Player, who just wants to get laid all the time. Also, there's a Lust demon in his head, invited by the Player in order to give him more leverage.<br /> <br /> What do you mean, &quot;it sounds like a metaphor for puberty&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T15:55:37-07:00","id":475003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=474771#post474771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the fact that if you give the vampire students an accessible means of rejuvenating their Vitae, then it takes a lot of tension out of the game by removing the need to make feeding rolls.<br /> <br /> Oh I'm sure you could justify making them from time to time, like after a big encounter, or if they've gone without for a while. But again, there's no reason for them to go without if they can just spend the $2.35 to buy a Vitae or two.<br /> <br /> Boarding school question's a good one. As are parents. I think some supers probably just don't have parents around as a rule (most Prometheans, Mummies, Demons, Changelings). Though those may have equivalents.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 2.35!? Where the heck do you live? Vending machines are only a dollar per drink here!<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I can imagine a gangrel coming home to their parents.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Dad, the kids at school picked on me for being poor&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> *Smacks the crap out of his kid*<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Harden up, boy!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-09-2015, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T16:02:01-07:00","id":475007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=475000#post475000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I want to run a Sin-Eater who's a hopeless romantic. Unfortunately, he happens to be sharing his body with a Geist known as the Player, who just wants to get laid all the time. Also, there's a Lust demon in his head, invited by the Player in order to give him more leverage.<br /> <br /> What do you mean, &quot;it sounds like a metaphor for puberty&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that our characters are polar oppsities while both being about the sexual/romantic part of puberty (with mine being about closeted nonhetero puberty in a non supportive family) obviously means that they will wind up being teamed up a lot by the storyteller, so maybe we should figure out what they think of each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T16:47:25-07:00","id":475062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=475003#post475003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> 2.35!? Where the heck do you live? Vending machines are only a dollar per drink here!<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I can imagine a gangrel coming home to their parents.<br /> <br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Dad, the kids at school picked on me for being poor&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> *Smacks the crap out of his kid*<br /> <br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Harden up, boy!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Gangrel's dad is Ken Titus?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/jKlhThmaB70\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/jKlhThmaB70\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/jKlhThmaB70\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/jKlhThmaB70 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=475007#post475007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that our characters are polar oppsities while both being about the sexual/romantic part of puberty (with mine being about closeted nonhetero puberty in a non supportive family) obviously means that they will wind up being teamed up a lot by the storyteller, so maybe we should figure out what they think of each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves and Sin-Eaters both patrol the borders between the Material and an Otherworld (Shadow and Underworld respectively) so there's common ground there.<br /> <br /> My character also wouldn't be interested in sex except with a loving long-term partner, so he'd be better able to understand asexuality than most IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T17:15:34-07:00","id":475087,"title":"","content":"On the parental front, it's not like parents aren't <i>flat out always not involved. </i>I know lots of kids who got on great with their parents and let them be involved. The well-adjusted, possibly a bitch queen of the school awakening only for her parents to breathe out in relief and go &quot;Oh dear god, we hoped so&quot; would be something that works well.<br /> <br /> I just don't personally believe that kids are that well-adjusted a lot of the time, and when the new stuff comes in, a lot of teens do stop talking to their parents about that sort of stuff. Add in the metaphors most monsters stand in for, and the norm goes for parents who just can't understand.<br /> <br /> Bitch-queen of the school becoming an enlightened master of the secret laws really sounds like a fun character, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T17:43:22-07:00","id":475106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=475062#post475062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Werewolves and Sin-Eaters both patrol the borders between the Material and an Otherworld (Shadow and Underworld respectively) so there's common ground there.<br /> <br /> My character also wouldn't be interested in sex except with a loving long-term partner, so he'd be better able to understand asexuality than most IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my character's case (and the case of most asexuals, including myself), he feels sexual <b>desire</b> but not <b>attraction </b>to other people. It's a theoretical possibility that he finds <b>something </b>attractive but simply has never encountered it and therefore doesn't know what it is (which would be one type of what is known as a gray asexual, meaning someone who might have sexual attraction under the right circumstances, but is asexual otherwise.)<br /> <br /> Xenu, your character, could be could be considered gray if he is <b>only </b>capable of feeling attraction within a strong relationship.<br /> <br /> But at the high school point in his life, my character has never experienced sexual attraction and finds the behavior of people who do to be utterly confusing. He doesn't get a lot of jokes or references about sex and he's only just starting to learn how much sex motivates the behavior of others, but he doesn't have any point of reference to compare that information to. Maybe finding out whether he is flat out asexual or gray (and if so, what it is that he is attracted to ) could be an aspiration for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T18:03:22-07:00","id":475140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=475087#post475087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The well-adjusted, possibly a bitch queen of the school awakening only for her parents to breathe out in relief and go &quot;Oh dear god, we hoped so&quot; would be something that works well.<br /> <br /> Bitch-queen of the school becoming an enlightened master of the secret laws really sounds like a fun character, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so I've got<br /> <br /> Me: Werewolf<br /> <br /> Arcane: possibly Mage<br /> <br /> Xenu: probably Sin-eater<br /> <br /> Any Changlings, Vampires, Demons, Hunters, Mummies or Prometheans?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T18:12:19-07:00","id":475145,"title":"","content":"I was thinking werewolf as well, but for diversity's sake we'll leave that with you.<br /> <br /> That still leaves me with Mage or Deceived, though Demon, Hunter, and Changeling are options for me for obvious reasons, if I may boast a little.<br /> <br /> If I do Mage, it will at least be a popular and more entitled character, though bitchiness is something I'm gonna poke at.*<br /> <br /> I'll come up with what sort of characters I'd do on the others.<br /> <br /> In fact, here's another one, because in roleplay I actually quite love playing tropes-Good Faithful Girl(Need to pick a faith, I might go straight for Christianity, but a Muslim would be fun, and lord knows I love me some Hindi's) on the edge of her Becoming, as changing into a Child of the Seventh Generation. Also coming to realize she's a lesbian.(Because, you know, tropes)<br /> <br /> If I get a friend in on this, he'd play a changeling and I'd play a normal girl who's also a track star.<br /> <br /> *Is it just me, or is the truth of the average school that the popular people got to be popular by also being really good and decent people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-09-2015, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T18:35:51-07:00","id":475183,"title":"","content":"I'd be a Mummy. Specifically a Tef-Aabhi. I said Maa-Kep earlier in the thread, but that's because I had them confused. Presumably some sort of Twice-Arisen, or he was Rite of Returned while young-looking enough to be a high-schooler.<br /> <br /> For whatever reason, during this Descent he will be attending high school. Either because the Judges said so, or because it's the Sothic Turn and that's just what he decided to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T18:41:19-07:00","id":475188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=475087#post475087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the parental front, it's not like parents aren't <i>flat out always not involved. </i>I know lots of kids who got on great with their parents and let them be involved. The well-adjusted, possibly a bitch queen of the school awakening only for her parents to breathe out in relief and go &quot;Oh dear god, we hoped so&quot; would be something that works well.<br /> <br /> I just don't personally believe that kids are that well-adjusted a lot of the time, and when the new stuff comes in, a lot of teens do stop talking to their parents about that sort of stuff. Add in the metaphors most monsters stand in for, and the norm goes for parents who just can't understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the parent front, I kind of agree. Depending on the supernatural and the level of Masquerade, an involved but highly ignorant parent couldmake for a much more interesting story than a totally uninvolved one.<br /> <br /> For example: a Demon whose cover was a teenage boy who was supposed to murder his parents then &quot;kill&quot; himself, but fell because his parents were just too damn loving. Now he has to keep his family safe from the G-M without tipping them off. The difficulty is compounded by the fact that they can't seem to understand that their &quot;little boy&quot; is in fact nearly an adult now, let alone a techgnostic demon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bitch-queen of the school becoming an enlightened master of the secret laws really sounds like a fun character, actually. </div> </div> </div>I was actually also planning to play a Mage (Free Council Obrimos prankster/social justice warrior/gadfly). One who'd probably want probably end up doing his damnedest to humiliate an alpha-bitch type, especially one who was also a Mage. At least at first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 04-09-2015, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T19:10:03-07:00","id":475213,"title":"","content":"Trope-wise, I'd be the rich foreign kid who doesn't really fit in and his parents have been in absentia but give him literally everything he wants or needs money-wise. Working on a big social project like prom would give him a chance to connect with people in a way that he never had and come out of his shell, just in time for his parents to come back from a long trip and pull him back home for being too willful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T19:15:23-07:00","id":475215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/461116-new-high-school-of-darkness?p=475213#post475213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trope-wise, I'd be the rich foreign kid who doesn't really fit in and his parents have been in absentia but give him literally everything he wants or needs money-wise. Working on a big social project like prom would give him a chance to connect with people in a way that he never had and come out of his shell, just in time for his parents to come back from a long trip and pull him back home for being too willful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a Mummy to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T19:34:19-07:00","id":475223,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I'm pretty sure that we've decided that the school is going to be a &quot;normal&quot; private school (with a mix of Gothic and modern architecture due to renovations) that has supernatural stuff under the surface. What we need to decide now is the nearby town that the students hang out in and the teachers live in. I personally want the school to be on one of the Georgia barrier islands.<br /> <br /> Preferably Tybee island, which has a great story hook in the form of a Mark 15 nuclear bomb that the air force accidentally dropped there back in the 50s and never recovered. It is also close to Savannah and all it's paranormal stuff (ask me about the tunnels beneath the city and the altar they found down there). It has a history of pirate activity (because pirate ghosts and pirate treasure are great hooks) and was a major resort spot, meaning that the Ashwood Abby/the Silver ladder/the Invictus/the Ivory Claws/ a long lost wealthy sin eater krewe/any wealthy splat might have left something there after a party long ago that needs to be taken care of.<br /> <br /> St. Simmons Island would be my 2nd choice, it is a hub of the African American Gullah culture which preserved many african rituals, words and folk tales despite slavery, home to many plantations (presumably haunted), a mass suicide of recently arrived slaves right before they banned the import of slaves from africa (presumably creating a haunting) and traditional home to two native american tribes with an interesting ritual,<br /> <br /> St. Catherines Island would make a good spot for a field trip. It is probably incredibly haunted and home to some powerful death and storm spirts due to the 1893 sea islands hurricane, which killed all but one person on the Island and destroyed every building, The fact that Island is mostly wilderness is good for nature type splats (St. Catherines is owned by a private research foundation and isn't open to the public, but I could see a wealthy private school being allowed a field trip) in fact, the barrier islands of Georgia were a birthplace of the ecology movement.<br /> <br /> And of course, putting the school and town on an Island makes it easier for the government to seal it all off when a paranormal disaster hits the Island...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T20:04